From 6657e4f78e3fc6efc50641ff7ccc4295f3dc3f0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romain Dolbeau <romain@dolbeau.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:10:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] virt68k: virtsmp(4), secondary CPU start, IPIs; MP-safe
 pmap (steps N2-N5)

- virtsmp(4) attaches from the BI_VIRT_SMP_BASE bootinfo record.  It
  provides a timecounter (also without MULTIPROCESSOR, where it only
  reports the CPUs).  With MULTIPROCESSOR it attaches the secondary
  CPUs (cpu_info, private vector table, scratch stack, mi_cpu_attach),
  starts them from cpu_boot_secondary_processors() through a locore
  trampoline that enables the MMU like the boot CPU, delivers IPIs
  (AST, xcall, ipi(9), halt, TLB shootdown) and drives hardclock() on
  the secondary CPUs from their per-CPU timers.
- pmap_motorola: one CADDR1/CADDR2 pair per CPU; with MULTIPROCESSOR,
  the entry points take the kernel lock (kenter/kremove and the kernel
  PT page lists a recursive spin lock), and TLB invalidations are
  broadcast to the other CPUs by IPI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
